{# CTEM hero artwork — three example topologies, played one after another.

   Line drawing on white (ink nodes, dashed zone outlines) with a single
   amber attack path per scene. Each scene is a full SVG stacked in the same
   stage; the script below cross-fades them every ~7 s and the CSS in
   /ctem.css draws the path in, lights the nodes it touches (delays via the
   --d custom property) and runs a travelling pulse along it.

   Scenes, mapped to the page copy:
     1  Pure IT chain. A staging host that appears in no inventory, and the
        path from it to the domain controller.
     2  IT chain plus cloud / identity provider. A leaked employee password
        entered at the IdP, no vulnerability needed.
     3  IT chain plus an OT zone. The same path toward a plant, stopped at
        the IT/OT boundary.

   Reduced motion: no cycling, scene 1 shown with the path fully drawn.
   Labels are locale-aware via `locale` (en | de). All SVGs are aria-hidden;
   the <figure> carries the accessible description.
#}
{% set TOPO = {
